0012:     - Background pixels form 4-connected regions: some are single intact cell interiors, others pass through gaps in the lattice.
0013:     Rule
0014:     - Preserve all non-background lattice pixels.
0015:     - For each 4-connected background region, compare its area with its inclusive bounding-box area.
0016:     - Recolor a region green when it exactly fills that rectangle; recolor it yellow when gaps connect multiple cells and leave lattice pixels inside its bounding box.
0017:     Key insight
0018:     - A single isolated cell is exactly a solid rectangle, while any open multi-cell area is a non-rectangular background component.
